      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "YAIRA DUBIN, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Assistant to the Solicitor General)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "YAIRA DUBIN, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Andy Warhol Foundation for the Visual Arts, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Both courts below agreed and Goldsmith doesn't dispute that Warhol's Prince Series can reasonably be perceived to convey a fundamentally different meaning or message from Goldsmith's photograph. The question in this case is whether that different meaning or message should play a role, any role, in the fair use analysis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Andy Warhol Foundation for the Visual Arts, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I want to emphasize three points. First, the precedent supports us. Campbell unambiguously requires an examination of meaning or message. Google reaffirms that test and cites Warhol's Soup Cans as a paradigmatic example of when it's satisfied. Goldsmith's test is at odds with both cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Could you give us an example of any follow-on work that fails your test?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Why? I mean, derivative works are generally in a different medium, and almost all of them, even a dramatization on -- on theater or even a motion picture or a sequel, they add something new according to your definition in your brief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, going back to your answer to Justice Kavanaugh and now to Justice Kagan, what's the right level of generality? You keep going back to the author's purpose, and I can't stay there because, when I look at Harper & Row, we defined the purpose of the use as news reporting. In Campbell, we repeatedly referred to the uses -- the use as its parody character. In Google, we talked about creating a new product that does something different."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: So, in other words, you would sue me?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Martinez",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that in -- in this kind of circumstance, I think this -- this is totally different because there is a transformative meaning or message and there's an enormous amount of creativity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Why would that be?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus brief",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One of the amicus briefs says your position poses an existential threat to photographers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, what's a --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Was it, Ms. Blatt --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: Ms. Blatt, can --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 77,
        "start": 77
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Suppose that the Mona Lisa was copyrighted and somebody, a real -- really skillful copyist, made almost an exact copy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0003-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: You're saying it's still necessary?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: But you're --so -- so you're -- the Second Circuit looked at this a certain way. And are you saying they -- they did it wrong?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0004-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BLATT: No, they did it absolutely correct because they were just rejecting the district court and saying, we're leaving open everything but something that says Prince looked iconic versus Prince looked shy based on these interpretations of what one might reasonably think of Prince's, I don't know, mood or something, or personality."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0004-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. DUBIN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Two questions drive Factor 1: Does the use serve a distinct purpose or instead supersede the original, and what is the justification for copying? Both point against fair use here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0005-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 109,
        "start": 109
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: I'm sorry. But that -- that -- that isn't helpful for me."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0005-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 112,
        "start": 112
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Can I -- can I just ask you about that? Because you said it wasn't necessary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0005-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 116,
        "start": 116
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: So you would leave out \"essential\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Roman Martinez",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0005-0008",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 122,
        "start": 122
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On consequences, it's really important to understand that the creation of the Warhol works is directly at play in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2c0420041b3de3da33bccc350397e4ebd43941902d0f2ad1c972b54551d17377",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2c0420041b3d-0005-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 124,
        "start": 124
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
